course: dictionary
lesson: 1270
title: Busily: working hard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Busily is an adverb, a word that tells you how something is done. In «the Rat is busily making four little heaps of weapons», busily tells you how the Rat is making them: in a busy way, working hard and actively.
explain: Busily often goes with action words like work, write, chatter and bustle. Ask yourself: does the word show how the action happens? To check your meaning, swap in another word, such as «actively». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Busily can also mean being very occupied with one task. In «the gardeners are busily painting them red», three people are fully focused on one job, so busily shows how hard they are working at it.
fact: Busily is an adverb, and it tells how or in what way something is done.
fact: It comes from the adjective busy. When -ly is added, the y changes to i: busy becomes busily.
fact: «Busily» means in a busy way: working hard and actively at something.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «busily engaged in» and «busily at work».
fact: The comparative and superlative forms are more busily and most busily.
exercise: «The Rat is busily making four little heaps of weapons.» Which word tells how the Rat is making them? | *busily | heaps | Rat | weapons
exercise: «The gardeners were busily painting the roses red.» What does busily mean here? | Sleeping quietly beside the roses | *Working hard at the task | Shouting loudly at the roses | Walking away from the garden
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to busily? | *actively | lazily | sadly | quietly
test: Which sentence uses busily correctly to show someone working hard? | The sky was busily blue. | The cat slept busily on the mat. | The bell rang busily at noon. | *The cook was busily chopping onions for the soup.
test: Ruby says busily means very quietly. What is the right meaning? | Sleepily, with eyes closed | *In a busy way, working hard and actively | Without making a sound | Far away from everyone
exam: In «The ants worked busily to carry crumbs home», which word is the adverb that tells how the ants worked? | *busily | ants | home | crumbs
